Real integrations must read responses and substitute returned IDs; these are not a complete working client.

Use the portable root `mcp.json` schema and explicit transport; for example (remote endpoint only):
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://agent-plugins.org/schemas/1.0.0/mcp.schema.json",
  "mcpServers": {
    "research": {
      "type": "streamable-http",
      "url": "https://example.invalid/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```
`.invalid` is intentionally nonfunctional. Local vs remote transport and authentication must be established in implementation.

```ts
import { Codex } from '@openai/codex-sdk';
const client = new Codex();
const thread = client.startThread();
const turn = await thread.run('Summarize this repository architecture');
console.log(turn.finalResponse);
const next = await thread.run('Identify architectural risks');
```

**[DOCUMENTED]** `startThread()` creates a thread; `resumeThread(id, options)` reconnects to a persisted conversation, subject to local session availability. `run()` returns completed turn data; `runStreamed()` yields structured events.

```ts
const thread = codex.startThread({
  model: process.env.CODEX_RESEARCH_MODEL,
  modelReasoningEffort: 'high',
  sandboxMode: 'read-only',
  approvalPolicy: 'on-request',
});
```
This configuration requests settings; it does not guarantee host acceptance.

```ts
async function processWorkUnit(work: WorkUnit) {
  const lease = await store.claim(work.id);
  const thread = codex.startThread({
    model: routing.choose(work.kind),
    sandboxMode: 'read-only',
  });
  const turn = await thread.run(buildTaskPrompt(lease), {
    outputSchema: schemas.forKind(work.kind),
  });
  const parsed = validateAgainstSchema(turn.finalResponse);
  await verifyEvidence(parsed);
  await store.commitResult(lease, parsed);
}
```
These helper names are **application-defined**, not SDK methods. Error handling, timeouts, renewals, cancellation and retries are omitted.

```ts
interface WorkUnit {
  id: string;
  kind: string;
  status: 'queued' | 'leased' | 'blocked' | 'complete' | 'failed';
  attempts: number;
  inputRefs: string[];
  outputRefs: string[];
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  leaseUntil?: string;
  version: number;
}
```
